# Caveman — Implementation Plan

## Context
Open-source Gmail-only email client. Convex backend, React frontend. ~10 users. Inbox zero + team collaboration.

---

## Phase 1: Foundation

### 1.1 Project Setup
- Init monorepo (pnpm or just flat)
- `npx create-convex` + React (Vite)
- TailwindCSS setup
- Deploy to Vercel or similar

### 1.2 Google OAuth
- Create GCP project + OAuth consent screen
- Configure Convex auth with Google provider
- Store Google refresh token in Convex `users` table on first login
- Scopes: `gmail.readonly`, `gmail.send`, `gmail.modify`

### 1.3 Convex Schema
```
users        — id, email, name, googleRefreshToken, settings
threads      — id, userId, gmailThreadId, subject, snippet, labelIds, lastMessageAt, isRead, isMuted, snoozedUntil
messages     — id, threadId, gmailMessageId, from, to, cc, body, date, attachments
labels       — id, userId, gmailLabelId, name, type (system/user)
syncState    — id, userId, historyId (for delta sync)
```

### 1.4 Initial Gmail Sync
- Convex action: exchange refresh token → access token
- Fetch all threads (paginated, most recent first)
- Store thread metadata + messages in Convex
- Save `historyId` for future delta sync

---

## Phase 2: Core Email

### 2.1 Inbox View
- Reactive query: threads where `INBOX` in labelIds, ordered by lastMessageAt
- Thread list component (sender, subject, snippet, time)
- Read/unread visual state

### 2.2 Thread View
- Click thread → show all messages in order
- Render HTML email bodies (sandboxed iframe or sanitized HTML)
- Mark as read on open (mutation + Gmail API call)

### 2.3 Compose & Reply
- Rich text editor (TipTap or similar)
- Compose new email → Gmail API `messages.send`
- Reply / Reply All / Forward
- Attachments upload

### 2.4 Basic Actions
- Archive (remove INBOX label)
- Delete (move to TRASH)
- Star / Unstar
- Label management

---

## Phase 3: Inbox Zero

### 3.1 Split Inbox
- User-configurable rules (by label, sender domain, etc.)
- Tab UI: Primary / Updates / Newsletters / etc.
- Each tab = filtered reactive query

### 3.2 Snooze
- `snoozedUntil` field on thread
- Hide from inbox view (query filter)
- Convex scheduled function: at snooze time → re-add INBOX label + clear snoozedUntil

### 3.3 Send Later
- Compose → store draft in Convex with `sendAt` timestamp
- Convex scheduled function: at sendAt → call Gmail API send → delete draft

### 3.4 Undo Send
- On send, delay actual Gmail API call by ~5 seconds
- Show undo toast → cancel the scheduled send
- If no undo → send fires

### 3.5 Mute
- `isMuted` flag on thread
- Muted threads hidden from inbox
- New messages in muted threads stay hidden

### 3.6 Reminders
- Set follow-up reminder on sent email
- Convex scheduled function: check if reply received → if not, resurface thread

---

## Phase 4: Real-time Sync

### 4.1 Pub/Sub Webhook
- Set up Google Cloud Pub/Sub topic + subscription
- Convex HTTP action as push endpoint
- On webhook: call `users.history.list(startHistoryId)` → apply deltas

### 4.2 Delta Sync
- Parse history response: messagesAdded, messagesDeleted, labelsAdded, labelsRemoved
- Apply changes to Convex tables
- Update syncState.historyId
- UI updates reactively (no polling)

### 4.3 Fallback Polling
- Convex cron: every 2 min, check history for each user
- Catches missed Pub/Sub events

---

## Phase 5: Collaboration

### 5.1 Schema Additions
```
teams        — id, name
teamMembers  — id, teamId, userId
sharedThreads — id, teamId, threadId, sharedBy
comments     — id, threadId, userId, body, createdAt
presence     — id, userId, threadId, isTyping, lastSeen
```

### 5.2 Shared Threads
- Share button → create sharedThread record
- Team members see shared threads in a "Shared" split
- Reactive: new messages appear for all team members

### 5.3 Comments
- Internal comment thread on any email thread
- Reactive query: all comments for a thread
- Not sent to email recipients

### 5.4 Typing Indicators
- Presence mutation: set isTyping when composing a reply
- Reactive query: show "X is replying..." in thread view
- Auto-expire after 5s of inactivity

---

## Implementation Order

```
Phase 1 (week 1-2)    → Foundation: setup, auth, schema, initial sync
Phase 2 (week 3-4)    → Core email: inbox, threads, compose, actions
Phase 3 (week 5-6)    → Inbox zero: split inbox, snooze, send later, mute
Phase 4 (week 7)      → Real-time sync: Pub/Sub, delta sync
Phase 5 (week 8-9)    → Collaboration: shared threads, comments, presence
```

